  "id": "thema",
  "term": "thema",
  "definition": "In this social-psychological context, a thema is a basic oppositional pattern of meaning that organizes how people understand an issue through communication, such as a Self/Other distinction. It shapes social representations and identity by linking concerns like risk to particular groups, often supporting stigma and blame toward marginalized out-groups.",
